# Consistent Comparisons between Monopoly and Perfect Competition.

**Authors:** Skeath, Susan E., And Others

## Abstract
Identifies inconsistencies in treatments of the perfect competition, monopoly welfare comparison in textbooks for economics instruction. Argues for explanation of how experiments are being conducted and explicit identification of all underlying assumptions. Suggests straightforward analysis of the social cost of monopoly based on a comparison between two long run equilibria under comparable cost conditions. (DK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ458443

